// "[subject] mills N" ([CR#701.17a]): the DECLARATIVE-SUBJECT mill — that
// player puts the top N cards of their library into their graveyard as one
// group; a single instruction, clamped to library size ([CR#701.17b]).
// `Mills`'s slice-family twin of `Mill`: a `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit
// `Composite` named "Mill" whose body is the top slice of `who`'s library
// (`whose: Param(0)`) moving to their graveyard. The engine reads the
// performer off the body's selection and commits the whole top slice as ONE
// simultaneous batch of per-card, individually-redirectable moves so "milled
// this way" reads find the cards ([CR#701.17c,616.1]).
//
// `who` (Param(0)) rides the group selection's `whose`. The template renders
// the subject context-aware ("Target player mills five cards."); the count
// spells its noun via the `card|cards` modifier.
//
// Usage: Mills(It, 5) (the announced player target, Tome Scour) /
// Mills(It, 20) (Jace Beleren).
(
    name: "Mills",
    template: "${0} mills ${1:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Reference, Count],
    body: Batch(Param(1), Composite(
        name: Mill,
        body: MoveGroup(
            group: TopOfLibrary(count: 1, whose: Param(0)),
            arrangement: AnyOrder,
            to: Graveyard,
        ),
    )),
)
